<rml>
<head>
	<!--
		The menu (ADR-0018 §1): pad Start, or Back's last level. It holds what is not about the building: Riprendi,
		Impostazioni and Esci, which asks once; each later step of I7 adds its section's button here. A game left running
		stays running.
		Bound to the data model "system_menu" of rv::ui::SystemMenuScreen (src/ui/src/system_menu_screen.cpp); its ids are
		rv::ui::elementIdOf()'s (src/ui/include/rv/ui/system_menu_model.hpp). view: main, confirm. The focus is the model's;
		the input stays with the application, a click presses a button (VR's ray too).
	-->
	<title>Menu</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="system_menu.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="system_menu">
	<div id="system-menu" class="panel">
		<div data-if="view == 'main'">
			<h1>Retroverse</h1>
			<button id="sm-resume" class="action primary" data-event-click="button('resume')">Riprendi</button>
			<button id="sm-settings" class="action" data-event-click="button('settings')">Impostazioni</button>
			<button id="sm-quit" class="action" data-event-click="button('quit')">Esci</button>
		</div>
		<div data-if="view == 'confirm'">
			<h1>Uscire da Retroverse?</h1>
			<p class="note">Un gioco lasciato in esecuzione resta aperto.</p>
			<button id="sm-stay" class="action primary" data-event-click="button('stay')">Annulla</button>
			<button id="sm-confirm-quit" class="action danger" data-event-click="button('confirm-quit')">Esci</button>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
